</span></div>
</figure>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">The Calculation of Covariance Flux.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given the last token hidden state set <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H^{l,k}=\{h_{i}^{l,k}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H^{l,k}=\{h_{i}^{l,k}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math> from layer <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>-shot ICL prompts, we recall the low-rank filter obtained in §<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1 Explicit Task-Verbalization Subspace in Zero-shot Hidden States ‣ 3 Task-oriented Information Removal towards TVS ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a> (independently trained from 0-shot setting) as <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{enc}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>enc</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{enc}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="W_{\text{dec}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">W_{\text{dec}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we calculate the mapped<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
                <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
                
                
                
              Notice that the bias terms in the linear layer do not affect the covariance, so we omit them here.</span></span></span> hidden state set as <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{1}^{l,k}=\{h_{i}^{l,k}W_{\text{enc}}W_{\text{dec}}\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>h</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>enc</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>W</mi><mtext>dec</mtext></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{1}^{l,k}=\{h_{i}^{l,k}W_{\text{enc}}W_{\text{dec}}\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, and calculate the covariance matrix of the mapped set as <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{1}^{l,k}=\mathrm{Cov}[H_{1}^{l,k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>H</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{1}^{l,k}=\mathrm{Cov}[H_{1}^{l,k}]</annotation></semantics></math>, also the covariance matrix of the original set as <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{l,k}=\mathrm{Cov}[H^{l,k}]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Cov</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{l,k}=\mathrm{Cov}[H^{l,k}]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, we calculate the covariance flux as:</p>
<table id="A1.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Covariance Flux}=\frac{\|D_{1}^{l,k}\|_{*}}{\|D^{l,k}\|_{*}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Covariance Flux</mtext><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Covariance Flux}=\frac{\|D_{1}^{l,k}\|_{*}}{\|D^{l,k}\|_{*}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where the <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|_{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|_{*}</annotation></semantics></math> is the nuclear norm, i.e., the sum of the singular values.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Experiment Details.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Based on the same 512-size test set with Appendix <a href="#A1.SS2" title="A.2 Training Details of 𝑊_enc⁢𝑊_dec (§) ‣ Appendix A Experiment Details ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">A.2</span></a>, we sample 2 demonstration sequence for each test sample with <math id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations. Then, on the specified layer, we extract the hidden states from these 1024 test samples to measure the 2 metrics.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Accuracy with Instruction and Label Configurations.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">As supplementary information, we list the accuracies in the input configurations shown in Fig. <a href="#S3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 3.2 LMs Intrinsically Recover TVS by Task-oriented Information Removal ‣ 3 Task-oriented Information Removal towards TVS ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> and <a href="#S3.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ 3.2 LMs Intrinsically Recover TVS by Task-oriented Information Removal ‣ 3 Task-oriented Information Removal towards TVS ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> in Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ A.3 Details for Experiment of § ‣ Appendix A Experiment Details ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.4 </span>Details for Attention Visualization in Fig. <a href="#S4.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ 4.1 Identify Denoising Heads ‣ 4 Denoising Heads for Task-oriented Information Removal ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a></h3>

<figure id="A1.F15" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A1.F15.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="205.9" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 205.9" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,205.9) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#404040;" fill="#404040" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 200 C 0 203.26 2.64 205.9 5.91 205.9 L 544.09 205.9 C 547.36 205.9 550 203.26 550 200 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2F2;" fill="#F2F2F2" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 200 C 1.97 202.17 3.73 203.93 5.91 203.93 L 544.09 203.93 C 546.27 203.93 548.03 202.17 548.03 200 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 16.47)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:12.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="178.35" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 175.66)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
