<div id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px12.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We repeat the experiment shown in Fig. <a href="#S4.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ 4.2 Analysis of Denoising Heads ‣ 4 Denoising Heads for Task-oriented Information Removal ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> and <a href="#S5.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ 5 Conclusion and Discussion ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> on Llama 3-8B, Qwen 2.5-3B and 7B as shown in Fig. <a href="#A6.F36" title="Figure 36 ‣ Augmentation Results for Fig. and (“Factor-recall Filter Injection”). ‣ Appendix F Augmentation Results ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a> and <a href="#A6.F36" title="Figure 36 ‣ Augmentation Results for Fig. and (“Factor-recall Filter Injection”). ‣ Appendix F Augmentation Results ‣ Mechanism of Task-oriented Information Removal in In-context Learning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">36</span></a>.</p>
</div>
